(D3 — Discrepancy 3 repro: a loop-expansion clause whose collection is a
 SCALAR used to be accepted with no diagnostic and segfaulted at runtime
 (exit 139, deterministic 60/60). The manual's "Supported collections"
 list (LANGUAGE.md:2803-2806) is lists, ranges and `arguments's all`; a
 number is none of those.
 **RESOLVED — fixed by vox #49 (0.4.8+).** The analyzer now refuses a
 non-list collection at compile time, so this two-token program no longer
 builds and no longer crashes. A named number gives the same refusal with
 the variable's name and a tailored hint; a text variable and a text
 literal are refused too ("Loop collection must be a list: text").
 Note: the caret this diagnostic prints can land in a comment rather than
 on the offending statement -- see Discrepancy 10 (`D10.vox`); the message
 itself is correct.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox D3.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   error: Loop collection must be a list: a number
   (no binary produced; compile error)
   hint: `each ... from` walks a list, a range, or `arguments's all`
)
print each part from 4.
